        "recommendation": "Both compatibility paths are correct today: `#[serde(alias = \"listen\")]` keeps existing `config.toml` files readable, and `#[serde(rename = \"customer_id\")]` (src/api.rs:10) keeps the partners' JSON unchanged. But the migration path was verified only by hand on staging (tasks 1.1 and 1.2), and the repository has no test. Add a unit test that `config::load` accepts both a file with `listen` and one with `bind_address`, and one that serializes `OrderResponse` and asserts the `customer_id` key, so that removing either attribute in a later cleanup fails the build instead of breaking old configuration files or partners' integrations (docs/api.md promises two releases of deprecation).",
